    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e5ac39a_6d36fc38",
        "filename": ".gn",
        "patchSetId": 98
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-12T20:58:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not *entirely* sure what you mean differentiating Skia standalone vs embedders. From what I understand both skia.gni and \u003cskia\u003e/.gn are used when building on the Skia CQ/CI. We tend to create the flags in gn/skia.gni with a default that most developers would find useful and then set them in our test configurations as appropriate.\n(e.g. https://github.com/google/skia/blob/d05a87d8c21873125ea76fa723a47739d230b701/infra/bots/recipe_modules/build/default.py#L148-L156)\n\nWe rarely set anything in //.gn as a result and I\u0027d like to keep it that way.",
      "parentUuid": "3fb55fa0_acfbd934",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "5f98f29e369956db62f919b74afef706b229e720",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "969d2857_164da6e3",
        "filename": ".gn",
        "patchSetId": 98
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 18384
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-13T14:47:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My goal is to achieve three things simultaneously:\n1. **Noop for Embedders:** No impact on embedders by default.\n2. **Local Dev Experience:** Enabled for Skia developers locally.\n3. **CI Coverage:** Enabled on Skia CQ.\n\nThe distinction here is that `.gn` and `gn/BUILDCONFIG.gn` are specific to Skia\u0027s standalone build definition. When an embedder imports Skia, they define their own `.gn` and never inherit ours.\n\nIf we move this logic entirely to CI recipes, we achieve (1) and (3), but lose (2). This creates a friction point where developers will hit memory safety errors on the CQ that they cannot reproduce locally without manually discovering and setting flags.\n\nI believe using `.gn` is the cleanest way to ensure local builds match CQ without affecting embedders. However, if you feel strongly about keeping `.gn` strict, I can move it to infra, though I\u0027d prefer to avoid the divergence between local and CI environments.\n\n(Note: In PS93, I relied on `skia_partition_alloc_dir` being defined only from Skia BUILDCONFIG to achieve this. That remains another possibility if you prefer.)",
      "parentUuid": "7e5ac39a_6d36fc38",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "5f98f29e369956db62f919b74afef706b229e720",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
